Team,

Before this becomes another standing report, can we answer the real question?

The same decline code can lead to a successful retry, an ATM attempt, a phone=
 call or lost activity. The possible stories are that most declines recover i=
mmediately, that poor explanations drive complaints more than the decline its=
elf, or that repeat declines cluster by card state or channel.

We looked at a version of this before. For the March 2020 review, please show=
 what changed and whether the earlier conclusion still holds. The operating t=
eams agree that more journeys are failing; they disagree on whether the custo=
mer, the bank or a downstream party owns the failure.

Please prepare a short decision pack with no more than five slides and an att=
ached evidence table. The output must help us decide which decline reasons ne=
ed rule, message or service changes.

Data available: transaction-level timestamps, channels, amounts, statuses and=
 error context; ATM attempts, host responses, PIN attempts, blocked-card stat=
e and latency; monthly account snapshots, status events, limits, product enro=
lments and signatories; customer contacts, complaints and suggestions.

Please state the limitation plainly: The data does not contain merchant termi=
nal logs or card-scheme dispute outcomes.

Thanks
